{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And let me eat from my son's game.</b> The alef is a sign of the object [=direct object marker], and the implicit element that follows it stands in place of the root alef, likewise \"אומרה לאל כלעי\" (Psalms 42:10)." "The dagesh in the nun of תברכני (Genesis 27:19) is due to the loss of the additional nun, like \"יסובבנהו\" (Deut. 32:10) and likewise \"ישחרונני\" (Hosea 5:15)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text appears to contain scribal errors: המדבד likely means המושיא (the object marker), and the quoted form in Psalms 42:10 appears garbled; the received text reads לאל חי. The forms cited (ואכלה, אומרה) are apparently archaic feminine or cohortative forms where a final heh replaces the expected alef of the root."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:03.469631224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}